# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   E Muller et al. (2021). Machine learning potentials for complex aqueous systems made simple.
#   Spiral (Imperial College London). doi:10.1073/pnas.2110077118  arXiv:2106.00048v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2106.00048v2 (sha256 b93e36e21c240321...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 565 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/muller2021.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: six committee NNPs (8 n2p2 Behler-Parrinello members,
# two hidden layers of 20 neurons, 12 bohr cutoff) trained by query by
# committee on about 300 structures selected from AIMD trajectories of
# aqueous systems with different reference functionals. Accuracy is
# summarized as RDF, VDOS and force scores (Fig. 2); species-resolved
# force RMSEs appear only in figure panels and are not encoded.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

###############################################################################
