###############################################################################
# Q10 -- Benchmark results (Q11 inference-cost properties inline)
###############################################################################

# No energy/force/stress accuracy metric is reported in a form the schema captures (see Q12).

###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Force RMSEs per species (e.g. 55.8, 29.7, 56.8 meV/A for the fluoride system) are printed in figure panels whose species labels do not extract unambiguously; RDF/VDOS/force scores are not schema metrics. Training-set sizes are approximate (about 300); no n.
# - The manifest lists the first author as 'E Muller'; the paper and CrossRef list Christoph Schran first.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/muller2021.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
